Task 1: Enable proxy modules in Apache
Description Task 1: Enable the proxy and proxy_http modules in Apache for Debian and Suse systems.

Task 2: Configure Apache locations using a template
Description Task 2: Use a Jinja2 template to configure Apache locations and ensure the template file is placed in the correct directory with proper permissions. Notify handlers to test the Apache configuration and to restart Apache after configuration changes.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook:
---
- name: Enable proxy modules in Apache
  block:
    - name: Enable proxy module on Debian
      ansible.builtin.apache2ctl:
        module: "proxy"
        config: "proxy"
      when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"
    - name: Enable proxy module on Suse
      ansible.builtin.apache2ctl:
        module: "proxy"
        config: "proxy"
      when: ansible_os_family == "Suse"
    - name: Enable proxy_http module on Debian
      ansible.builtin.apache2ctl:
        module: "proxy_http"
        config: "proxy_http"
      when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"
    - name: Enable proxy_http module on Suse
      ansible.builtin.apache2ctl:
        module: "proxy_http"
        config: "proxy_http"
      when: ansible_os_family == "Suse"

- name: Configure Apache locations using a template
  block:
    - name: Ensure template file exists
      ansible.builtin.template:
        src: "templates/apache_locations.conf.j2"
        dest: "/etc/apache2/sites-available/locations.conf"
        owner: root
        group: root
        mode: "0644"
    - name: Ensure template file exists
      ansible.builtin.template:
        src: "templates/apache_locations.conf.j2"
        dest: "/etc/httpd/conf.d/locations.conf"
        owner: root
        group: root
        mode: "0644"
      when: ansible_os_family == "Suse"
  notify:
    - test_apache_configuration
    - restart_apache_server


